1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Pharma teams need to connect evidence scattered across research papers.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,977
This tool can support R and D with target research,

3
00:00:08,977 --> 00:00:10,966
clinical development with trial comparisons,

4
00:00:10,966 --> 00:00:14,000
and medical affairs with cited answers.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,608
Market access teams can compare outcomes,

6
00:00:16,608 --> 00:00:22,000
while safety and regulatory reviewers can trace literature findings back to sources.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,218
Hybrid Graph RAG links studies through shared concepts,

8
00:00:25,218 --> 00:00:26,827
then ranks relevant passages.

9
00:00:26,827 --> 00:00:31,000
This supports cross-study comparisons and counts beyond similarity search alone.

10
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Better retrieval still needs validation against a vector-only baseline.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:37,074
Start by searching PubMed.

12
00:00:37,074 --> 00:00:41,000
Click Ingest to add matching papers.

13
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:41,457
Here,

14
00:00:41,457 --> 00:00:44,197
papers increase from three to seven.

15
00:00:44,197 --> 00:00:48,000
Section-aware text chunks grow from ten to thirty-two.

16
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,830
Extract entities and PICO fields.

17
00:00:50,830 --> 00:00:55,000
Normalize synonyms to avoid duplicate concept nodes.

18
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,906
Graph edges rise from thirty-four to eighty-eight,

19
00:00:57,906 --> 00:01:00,398
normalized entities from eighteen to thirty-two,

20
00:01:00,398 --> 00:01:04,000
and thematic communities from five to eight.

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,050
The graph view expands from twenty-one to thirty-nine nodes,

22
00:01:08,050 --> 00:01:10,000
connecting studies and concepts.

23
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,233
Ask questions in Chat, or browse conditions, drugs,

24
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:15,000
and outcomes through NER.

25
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Use the PICO grid to compare populations, interventions, comparators, and outcomes, then export evidence.

26
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:22,474
Finally,

27
00:01:22,474 --> 00:01:25,318
inspect the evidence table and citations.

28
00:01:25,318 --> 00:01:30,000
Trace each finding back to its supporting source sentence.
